        "id": 1001591
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-26T23:23:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Despite this comment, I\u0027m not sure I understand the rationale of the caching strategy? Samplers are added to the cache but never retrieved, and the cache is only cleared on device destroy. I guess that implies that you expect a fairly low number of unique samplers in this context, and are relying on the frontend de-duplication? Wouldn\u0027t the front end cache already be keeping them alive, though?",
      "revId": "60fe67734a27bf1c642912d28c24990a5927d56d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "602a4e9f_2c517bbc",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/SamplerVk.h",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-27T18:39:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The frontend cache uses `ContentlessObjectCache` that doesn\u0027t keep the object alive but instead [keeps `WeakRefs`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/common/ContentLessObjectCache.h;drc\u003d9da3eaf710d7c5ae6c81f2a6af42b078ecab3b40;l\u003d231). That means that if an object is added to the cache, then dropped, it will be destroyed before we have a chance to use it.\n\nExpanded the comment a bit in the new patchset.",
      "parentUuid": "cc616793_bea31a3b",
      "revId": "60fe67734a27bf1c642912d28c24990a5927d56d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
